<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muscovite–Lithuanian War (1500–1503)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a>–<a href="/years/1503">1503</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscovite-lithuanian-wars">Muscovite–Lithuanian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muscovite–Lithuanian War of 1500–1503 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-jagiellon">Alexander Jagiellon</a>, after border princes changed allegiance to Moscow. The Muscovites won a major victory at Vedrosha in 1500, while their Livonian allies fought on a second front. The truce of 1503 left Moscow about a third of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>'s eastern territories.</p></div>
